-- allium: 3
-- interaction-capture.allium
--
-- Browser extension that records a user's interaction with the open
-- web page and writes it down as a PiX interaction score
-- (a 3- or 5-layer "partitura" of User / Dialogue / System / ...).
--
-- The unified library that hosts both authored scores and recordings
-- is the @pix/editor library at packages/editor (canonical store: the
-- editor's IndexedDB). The walkthrough viewer that surfaces the
-- screenshot trace of a recording is specified separately in
-- packages/editor/walkthrough-viewer.allium.
--
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Scope
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Included:
--   - Recording lifecycle: start, stop, pause, resume.
--   - Capture granularity: one ScoreStep + one TraceSnapshot per
--     accepted interaction event. Triggers vary by element kind:
--     click for buttons/links, blur-with-change for text inputs,
--     change for dropdown/checkbox/radio/file, plus drag-drop and
--     media playback start.
--   - Screenshot of the visible viewport plus a normalised focus
--     region that highlights the targeted element.
--   - Mapping captured action -> PiX score column with one cell per
--     visible layer, seeded with a pixogram inferred from the
--     element kind and a verb chosen by the interaction trigger.
--   - Section divisions: when a captured step lands on a different
--     "screen" (URL, document title, or browser tab) than the
--     previous step, the new step's step_title is seeded with the
--     screen's name so the editor renders a section divider.
--   - System events as steps: visible error UI (alert dialogs,
--     role="alert", aria-live="assertive", validation messages)
--     creates its own step in the system layer, anchored to the
--     URL where the error appeared.
--   - Hover-revealed content as annotations: when the user dwells
--     long enough on an element that reveals a tooltip / popover,
--     the revealed text is appended to the most recent step's note.
--   - Media playback: a video or audio that begins playing creates
--     its own step, captured once at play-start (later pause/seek
--     not captured to avoid step explosion).
--   - Multi-site continuity: top-level navigations (including
--     cross-origin hops to a payment gateway and back) do not
--     interrupt recording. The TraceSnapshot that lands on a new
--     host is tagged boundary = crossing.
--   - Multi-tab continuity: clicks in any tab opened from a recorded
--     page (target=_blank, window.open, ctrl-click) continue to
--     append to the same active recording. Each snapshot records
--     its tab identity so the walkthrough viewer can surface
--     parallel flows.
--   - Forensic posture: capture-derived data lives in a separate
--     ScreenshotTrace entity per Score; once written, snapshots are
--     append-only. Per-Score provenance metadata at create time.
--   - Local-only library (browser storage), survives browser restart.
--     The canonical store is the editor's IndexedDB; recordings are
--     flushed there on UserStopsRecording.
--   - Score state {draft | final}: recordings start as draft and
--     stay draft until the user explicitly promotes them.
--   - Export to two formats: PiX-JSON (round-trip with editor) and
--     a step-by-step tutorial PDF (driven by the ScreenshotTrace).
--
-- Excluded:
--   - All pictos.cl integration: aid-availability checks, in-page aid
--     overlay, sidepanel iframe to app.pictos.cl, "send task" upload,
--     and pictogram fetching from api.pictos.cl. This branch is offline.
--   - Browser-extension plumbing details (manifest shape, message bus,
--     service-worker lifetime). The browser is modelled as an external
--     boundary; specifics live in implementation, not in this spec.
--   - The PiX editor application itself (eadpucv/pix). This spec consumes
--     PiX's score data contract (layouts, layers, pixograms) as an
--     external vocabulary; that project owns it. The walkthrough viewer
--     for the screenshot trace is specified in
--     packages/editor/walkthrough-viewer.allium.
--   - Storage backend choice. The spec only commits to "local to the
--     browser profile, persistent across sessions, never on the network".
--   - Tamper-evidence beyond append-only semantics: no hash chains, no
--     digital signatures, no trusted timestamping.
--   - Audit log of exports: exporting a Score does not mutate it.
--   - Capture of typed input values verbatim: the dialogue cell
--     describes what the user did (Escribir en email), not what they
--     typed. Password fields never reveal anything beyond the fact
--     of typing. Dropdown / checkbox / radio selections do reveal
--     the chosen option label (it is meta-data, not free text).
--
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Library locus and storage
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The editor's IndexedDB is the canonical home for both authored scores
-- and recordings. The extension does not maintain a long-term score
-- library of its own; it owns the active recording session and flushes
-- its product to the editor library on UserStopsRecording.
--
-- Authored scores are created by the editor and start at state = final.
-- Recordings are created by the extension and start at state = draft.
-- A Score's state changes only via UserMarksScoreAsFinal /
-- UserReopensScoreAsDraft.
--
-- Each Recording owns a ScreenshotTrace 1:1, holding the screenshots
-- and focus regions that were captured. The Score itself is purely
-- the partitura — text and pixogram cells — so it can be edited
-- without ever touching the trace.

-- ============================================================
-- External Entities
-- ============================================================

-- The web page the user is interacting with. The extension observes
-- it; it does not own its lifecycle.
external entity WebPage {
    url: String
    title: String                           -- document.title at observation time
    viewport_width: Integer
    viewport_height: Integer
    tab_id: TabId                           -- which browser tab this page is in
}

-- A DOM element on the current page that the recorder considers
-- worth capturing. "Worth capturing" is defined by the
-- ElementInteractivityCriteria invariant.
external entity InteractiveElement {
    page: WebPage
    tag_name: String                        -- button | a | input | select | textarea | ...
    role: String?                           -- ARIA role, if any
    text_content: String?                   -- visible text inside the element
    aria_label: String?
    placeholder: String?                    -- for inputs
    selected_option_text: String?           -- for <select> with a current selection
    bounding_box: BoundingBox               -- position and size within the viewport
}

-- A media element (HTML <video> or <audio>) the user starts playing.
external entity MediaElement {
    page: WebPage
    tag_name: String                        -- "video" or "audio"
    src: String
    label: String?                          -- title attribute, aria-label, or filename
    bounding_box: BoundingBox
}

-- A visible error indicator on a page — a validation message, alert
-- dialog, role="alert" notification or similar. Detection criteria
-- live in @invariant ErrorDetectionCriteria.
external entity ErrorIndicator {
    page: WebPage
    text: String                            -- the visible error message
    severity: ErrorSeverity
    role_or_aria: String?                   -- e.g., 'role=alert', 'aria-live=assertive'
    bounding_box: BoundingBox?
}

-- A pixogram from the PiX icon vocabulary (160 monochrome SVG icons).
-- Identified by name only ("button", "input", "think", "process", ...).
external entity Pixogram {
    name: String
}

-- A serialized PiX score, conforming to the data contract owned by
-- @pix/core. Designed to open directly in the PiX web editor.
-- Screenshots and other capture-derived data are NOT part of the
-- score document — they live in the ScreenshotTrace.
external entity PiXScoreDocument {
    score_id: String                        -- target Score.id
    payload: String                         -- the JSON document (no screenshots)
}

-- A step-by-step tutorial PDF generated from a Score's ScreenshotTrace.
external entity TutorialPdf {
    score_id: String
    payload: Bytes
}

-- ============================================================
-- Value Types
-- ============================================================

value BoundingBox {
    x: Integer                              -- pixels from viewport left
    y: Integer                              -- pixels from viewport top
    width: Integer
    height: Integer
}

-- A single (layer x step) cell in a score. PiX renders cells as
-- "<pixogram> <text>". An absent cell has icon = null and text = "".
value Cell {
    icon: Pixogram?
    text: String
}

-- The highlighted region drawn over the screenshot in the viewer.
-- Stored as percentages of the screenshot dimensions so the highlight
-- survives image resizing.
value FocusRegion {
    x_percent: Decimal                      -- 0..100, centre x as % of width
    y_percent: Decimal                      -- 0..100, centre y as % of height
    radius_percent: Decimal                 -- 0..100, as % of half the longest edge
}

-- Provenance metadata captured once at Score creation.
value ScoreProvenance {
    user_agent: String
    extension_version: String
    timezone: String                        -- IANA name, e.g. "America/Santiago"
    locale: String                          -- BCP-47 tag, e.g. "es-CL"
}

-- Opaque identifier for a browser tab. The recorder uses this to
-- annotate snapshots and detect tab switches; the value itself is
-- meaningless outside the recording session.
value TabId {
    -- Implementation: chrome.tabs.Tab.id (an integer per session) or
    -- equivalent. The spec only requires uniqueness within the
    -- session and stability across the life of one tab.
}

-- ============================================================
-- Enumerations
-- ============================================================

-- The five PiX layers.
enum ScoreLayer {
    user | dialogue | system | environment | supporting_processes
}

enum ScoreLayout {
    pix                                     -- 3 layers: user, dialogue, system
    | sb                                    -- 5 layers: + environment, supporting_processes
}

enum ScoreState {
    draft                                   -- needs human refinement
    | final                                 -- authored or promoted
}

-- How the recorder classified the targeted element. Drives the
-- pixogram seeded into the dialogue cell.
enum CapturedElementKind {
    button | link | text_input | password_input | checkbox | radio
    | dropdown | text_area | file_input | media | drag_source
    | drag_target | error_surface | generic
}

-- What kind of interaction triggered the capture. Drives the verb
-- chosen for the dialogue cell text. Orthogonal to CapturedElementKind:
-- the same element kind can produce different InteractionTriggers
-- (a checkbox can be triggered by `change`, but never by `click_only`
-- — see @invariant TriggerMatchesKind).
enum InteractionTrigger {
    click                                   -- mouse click on a clickable element
    | text_committed                        -- input/textarea blurred with value changed
    | selection_committed                   -- dropdown/checkbox/radio changed
    | file_attached                         -- <input type=file> received a file
    | drag_drop                             -- source dragged and dropped on target
    | media_play                            -- <video>/<audio> started playing
    | system_error                          -- error UI became visible (system-emitted)
}

enum ErrorSeverity {
    error | warning | info
}

-- Marks a TraceSnapshot that landed on a different host than the
-- previous snapshot in its trace.
enum BoundaryMarker {
    none                                    -- same host as previous, or first snapshot
    | crossing                              -- this snapshot's host differs
}

-- ============================================================
-- Entities and Variants
-- ============================================================

-- The single global recording state for the extension. There is one
-- recorder per browser profile.
entity Recorder {
    state: idle | recording | paused
    active_score: Score?
    active_tab: TabId?                      -- the tab where the most recent capture occurred

    transitions state {
        idle -> recording                   -- UserStartsRecording
        recording -> paused                 -- UserPausesRecording
        paused -> recording                 -- UserResumesRecording
        recording -> idle                   -- UserStopsRecording
        paused -> idle                      -- UserStopsRecording (from paused)
    }
}

-- A PiX score. Owned and edited locally; never uploaded anywhere.
entity Score {
    id: UUID
    title: String
    description: String
    layout: ScoreLayout
    state: ScoreState
    movements: List<Movement> with score = this
    trace: ScreenshotTrace?                 -- absent for authored scores
    provenance: ScoreProvenance
    created_at: Timestamp
    updated_at: Timestamp

    visible_layers:
        if layout = pix:
            { user, dialogue, system }
        else:
            { environment, user, dialogue, system, supporting_processes }

    active_movement: movements.last
    total_steps: movements.sum(m => m.steps.count)
}

entity Movement {
    id: UUID
    score: Score
    position: Integer                       -- 0-based index within score.movements
    steps: List<ScoreStep> with movement = this
}

-- One column of the PiX grid — partitura content only. Capture-derived
-- data lives in the matching TraceSnapshot.
entity ScoreStep {
    id: UUID
    movement: Movement
    position: Integer                       -- 0-based index within movement.steps
    step_title: String                      -- non-empty marks the start of a section
    note: String                            -- caption below the grid; can include
                                            -- hover-reveal annotations and error context

    user_cell: Cell
    dialogue_cell: Cell
    system_cell: Cell
    environment_cell: Cell
    supporting_cell: Cell
}

-- The collection of captured snapshots for a recorded Score. Authored
-- scores have no trace; recordings have exactly one (1:1 with Score).
entity ScreenshotTrace {
    id: UUID
    score: Score
    snapshots: List<TraceSnapshot> with trace = this
    created_at: Timestamp
}

-- The empirical record of one captured interaction.
entity TraceSnapshot {
    id: UUID
    trace: ScreenshotTrace
    step: ScoreStep                         -- referenced by step.id

    screenshot: String                      -- data URL of the viewport
    focus: FocusRegion
    captured_at: Timestamp
    captured_from_url: String
    captured_page_title: String
    captured_tab_id: TabId
    captured_kind: CapturedElementKind
    captured_trigger: InteractionTrigger
    boundary: BoundaryMarker
}

-- ============================================================
-- Config
-- ============================================================

config {
    -- Pixogram names seeded into the dialogue cell, by element kind.
    icon_button: String = "button"
    icon_link: String = "link"
    icon_text_input: String = "input"
    icon_password_input: String = "password"
    icon_checkbox: String = "checkbox"
    icon_radio: String = "radioselect"
    icon_dropdown: String = "select"
    icon_text_area: String = "text"
    icon_file_input: String = "attach"
    icon_drag: String = "drag"
    icon_drop: String = "drop"
    icon_media_play: String = "play"
    icon_error: String = "alert"
    icon_generic_click: String = "click"

    -- Pixogram seeded into the system cell when the URL changed
    -- since the previous captured step.
    icon_navigation: String = "page"

    score_library_capacity: Integer = 20

    -- Debounce window for re-scanning interactive elements after
    -- DOM mutations. Below this, mutation bursts are coalesced.
    interactive_rescan_debounce: Duration = 300.milliseconds

    -- A hover that reveals a tooltip/popover only counts as a
    -- capture-worthy "hover reveal" if the user dwells this long.
    hover_capture_threshold: Duration = 1500.milliseconds

    -- Errors observed within this window of one another are
    -- coalesced into a single SystemErrorCapturesStep firing
    -- (so a validation that surfaces 3 messages at once becomes
    -- one step, not three).
    error_coalesce_window: Duration = 500.milliseconds
}

-- ============================================================
-- Defaults
-- ============================================================

default Cell empty_cell = { icon: null, text: "" }

-- ============================================================
-- Rules
-- ============================================================

rule UserCreatesScore {
    when: UserCreatesScore(layout, title?)

    requires: Score.count < config.score_library_capacity

    -- Authored scores skip the draft phase; they have no trace.
    ensures:
        let score = Score.created(
            id: new_uuid(),
            title: title ?? "",
            description: "",
            layout: layout,
            state: final,
            trace: null,
            provenance: capture_provenance(),
            created_at: now,
            updated_at: now
        )
        Movement.created(
            id: new_uuid(),
            score: score,
            position: 0
        )
}

rule UserStartsRecording {
    when: UserStartsRecording(score)

    requires: Recorder.state = idle
    requires: score.state = draft
    requires: exists score.trace

    ensures: Recorder.state = recording
    ensures: Recorder.active_score = score
}

rule UserPausesRecording {
    when: UserPausesRecording

    requires: Recorder.state = recording

    -- While paused, no capture event of any kind produces a step.
    -- The active_score is preserved so resume can continue. Per
    -- @guarantee RecordingStateAlwaysVisible, the overlay reflects
    -- the paused state distinctly from recording (e.g., the dot
    -- stops pulsing).
    ensures: Recorder.state = paused
}

rule UserResumesRecording {
    when: UserResumesRecording

    requires: Recorder.state = paused
    requires: exists Recorder.active_score

    ensures: Recorder.state = recording
}

rule UserStopsRecording {
    when: UserStopsRecording

    requires: Recorder.state = recording or Recorder.state = paused

    ensures: Recorder.state = idle
    ensures: Recorder.active_score = null

    -- The recording (Score + ScreenshotTrace) is persisted to the
    -- editor's canonical library at the moment the recorder stops.
    -- See @guarantee RecordingPersistedOnStop. The Score's state
    -- remains draft until UserMarksScoreAsFinal fires.
    ensures:
        RecordingFlushedToLibrary.applied(
            score: previously_active_score,
            policy: persist_score_and_trace
        )
}

-- The capture rules. Every accepted firing produces exactly one
-- ScoreStep + one TraceSnapshot, except UserHoverRevealsContent
-- (annotates an existing step) — see @invariant CaptureGranularity.
--
-- The shared structure:
--   * derive interaction kind, element kind, trigger
--   * compute dialogue text from auto_caption (per-trigger verb
--     mapping; NEVER includes typed text from <input> values; DOES
--     include selected option text from dropdown/checkbox/radio)
--   * detect section break (URL/title/tab change vs previous snapshot)
--   * detect boundary crossing (host change)
--   * build the step + snapshot

rule UserClickCapturesStep {
    when: UserClicksElement(element)

    requires: Recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists Recorder.active_score
    -- Click is the trigger for elements whose primary interaction is
    -- the click itself: buttons, links, generic clickables. Inputs
    -- and selectors have their own dedicated triggers below.
    requires: classify_element(element) in
        { button, link, generic, drag_source }

    let trigger = click
    let element_kind = classify_element(element)

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            score: Recorder.active_score,
            element: element,
            element_kind: element_kind,
            trigger: trigger
        )
}

rule UserTextInputCapturesStep {
    when: UserBlursTextInput(element, text_changed: Boolean)

    -- Text inputs (single-line, multi-line, password, contenteditable)
    -- capture on blur, only if the value changed during the focus
    -- session. This matches the user's intent: they wrote something.
    -- A pure focus-then-blur with no change does not capture.
    requires: Recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists Recorder.active_score
    requires: text_changed = true
    requires: classify_element(element) in
        { text_input, password_input, text_area }
        or element.is_contenteditable

    let trigger = text_committed

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            score: Recorder.active_score,
            element: element,
            element_kind: classify_element(element),
            trigger: trigger
        )
}

rule UserSelectionCapturesStep {
    when: UserChangesSelection(element, new_value)

    -- Dropdowns (<select>, role=listbox/combobox), checkboxes (and
    -- toggle switches), radios. Capture fires on the change event,
    -- when the value flips. The new value is included verbatim in
    -- the dialogue text — for these kinds it is choice meta-data,
    -- not free user input.
    requires: Recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists Recorder.active_score
    requires: classify_element(element) in
        { dropdown, checkbox, radio }

    let trigger = selection_committed

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            score: Recorder.active_score,
            element: element,
            element_kind: classify_element(element),
            trigger: trigger
        )
}

rule UserFileAttachmentCapturesStep {
    when: UserAttachesFile(element, file_count, file_names)

    requires: Recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists Recorder.active_score
    requires: classify_element(element) = file_input

    let trigger = file_attached

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            score: Recorder.active_score,
            element: element,
            element_kind: file_input,
            trigger: trigger
        )
}

rule UserDragDropCapturesStep {
    when: UserDragsAndDrops(source: InteractiveElement, target: InteractiveElement)

    -- A drag-drop is a single event with two participants. The step
    -- is anchored to the target (where the drop happened); the
    -- source identity is preserved in the dialogue text
    -- ("Arrastrar source a target"). The screenshot captures the
    -- viewport at the moment of drop; the focus region is on the
    -- target's bounding box.
    requires: Recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists Recorder.active_score

    let trigger = drag_drop

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            score: Recorder.active_score,
            element: target,
            element_kind: drag_target,
            trigger: trigger,
            secondary_element: source        -- consumed by auto_caption
        )
}

rule UserMediaPlaybackCapturesStep {
    when: MediaElementBeganPlaying(media: MediaElement)

    -- The user observed a video / audio start playing. Captured
    -- once at play-start. Subsequent pause / seek / end do not
    -- create steps (would explode the partitura on long media).
    -- The user can manually annotate the note if a specific
    -- moment of playback was meaningful.
    requires: Recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists Recorder.active_score

    let trigger = media_play

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            score: Recorder.active_score,
            element: media,                  -- treated as InteractiveElement-like
            element_kind: media,
            trigger: trigger
        )
}

rule SystemErrorCapturesStep {
    when: ErrorBecameVisible(indicator: ErrorIndicator)

    -- A visible error UI on a recorded page becomes its own step.
    -- The dialogue cell shows the error text with the alert
    -- pixogram. The system cell echoes pix-alert (the system is
    -- speaking). The user_cell remains empty — what the user
    -- felt is for the human author to describe.
    --
    -- Coalescing: errors that surface within
    -- config.error_coalesce_window of one another collapse into
    -- one step, with their texts joined.
    requires: Recorder.state = recording
    requires: exists Recorder.active_score

    let trigger = system_error

    ensures:
        capture_step(
            score: Recorder.active_score,
            element: indicator,
            element_kind: error_surface,
            trigger: trigger
        )
}

rule UserHoverRevealsContent {
    when: HoverRevealedContent(element, revealed_text, duration: Duration)

    -- A hover that reveals a tooltip / popover for at least
    -- config.hover_capture_threshold annotates the most recent
    -- step's note. It does NOT create a new step — hover is
    -- auxiliary information, not a moment of interaction.
    --
    -- If no step exists yet (the user hasn't done anything else),
    -- the hover is silently dropped (no anchor for the annotation).
    requires: Recorder.state = recording
    requires: duration >= config.hover_capture_threshold
    requires: revealed_text is non_empty

    let last_step = Recorder.active_score.active_movement.steps.last

    ensures:
        if last_step != null:
            last_step.note = append_hover_annotation(last_step.note, revealed_text)
            Recorder.active_score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserStartsNewMovement {
    when: UserStartsNewMovement(score)

    requires: Recorder.state = recording
    requires: Recorder.active_score = score

    ensures:
        Movement.created(
            id: new_uuid(),
            score: score,
            position: score.movements.count
        )
        score.updated_at = now
}

-- Manual editor actions (no click capture involved).

rule UserAddsBlankStep {
    when: UserAddsBlankStep(movement)

    -- Manually-added steps have no matching TraceSnapshot.
    ensures:
        ScoreStep.created(
            id: new_uuid(),
            movement: movement,
            position: movement.steps.count,
            step_title: "",
            note: "",
            user_cell: empty_cell,
            dialogue_cell: empty_cell,
            system_cell: empty_cell,
            environment_cell: empty_cell,
            supporting_cell: empty_cell
        )
        movement.score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserEditsCell {
    when: UserEditsCell(step, layer, new_value)

    ensures:
        if layer = user:                step.user_cell = new_value
        else if layer = dialogue:       step.dialogue_cell = new_value
        else if layer = system:         step.system_cell = new_value
        else if layer = environment:    step.environment_cell = new_value
        else:                           step.supporting_cell = new_value
        step.movement.score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserEditsScoreMetadata {
    when: UserEditsScoreMetadata(score, title?, description?, layout?)

    ensures:
        if exists title:        score.title = title
        if exists description:  score.description = description
        if exists layout:       score.layout = layout
        score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserDeletesStep {
    when: UserDeletesStep(step)

    ensures: not exists step
    ensures:
        for s in step.movement.score.trace?.snapshots where s.step = step:
            not exists s
    ensures: step.movement.score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserDeletesScore {
    when: UserDeletesScore(score)

    requires: Recorder.active_score != score

    ensures: not exists score
    ensures:
        if exists score.trace:
            not exists score.trace
            for s in score.trace.snapshots:
                not exists s
}

-- Score state transitions (draft <-> final).

rule UserMarksScoreAsFinal {
    when: UserMarksScoreAsFinal(score)

    requires: score.state = draft

    ensures: score.state = final
    ensures: score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserReopensScoreAsDraft {
    when: UserReopensScoreAsDraft(score)

    requires: score.state = final

    ensures: score.state = draft
    ensures: score.updated_at = now
}

rule UserDeletesTrace {
    when: UserDeletesTrace(score)

    requires: exists score.trace

    ensures: not exists score.trace
    ensures: score.trace = null
    ensures: score.updated_at = now
}

-- Export and re-import.

rule UserExportsScoreAsPiXJson {
    when: UserExportsScoreAsPiXJson(score)

    ensures:
        PiXScoreDocument.emitted(
            score_id: score.id,
            payload: pix_json_of(
                score: score,
                with_uuids: true
            )
        )
}

rule UserExportsScoreAsPdf {
    when: UserExportsScoreAsPdf(score)

    ensures:
        TutorialPdf.emitted(
            score_id: score.id,
            payload: pdf_tutorial_of(
                score: score,
                trace: score.trace,
                page_per_snapshot: true,
                instruction_text_source: "dialogue_cell.text"
            )
        )
}

rule UserImportsPiXScore {
    when: UserImportsPiXScore(target_score, document)

    requires: target_score.id = document.score_id

    -- The trace is NEVER touched by re-import — the document never
    -- carries snapshots. Replace-in-place applies to partitura
    -- fields only.
    ensures:
        ReconcilePiXDocument.applied(
            target: target_score,
            document: document,
            policy: replace_in_place_preserve_trace
        )
        target_score.updated_at = now
}

-- ============================================================
-- Invariants
-- ============================================================

@invariant ElementInteractivityCriteria
    -- An InteractiveElement is one for which any of the following holds:
    --   1. tag_name in {button, a, input, select, textarea}
    --   2. ARIA role in {button, link, checkbox, radio, menuitem, tab,
    --      listbox, option, switch, searchbox, textbox, combobox}
    --   3. has an onclick attribute, or is an `a` with an href
    --   4. has tabindex other than -1
    --   5. has contenteditable = "true"
    -- Open and closed shadow roots are traversed. The set is rebuilt
    -- on DOM mutations, debounced by interactive_rescan_debounce.

@invariant ErrorDetectionCriteria
    -- An ErrorIndicator becomes visible when a DOM element matches
    -- ANY of:
    --   1. role = "alert" or role = "alertdialog"
    --   2. aria-live = "assertive" with non-empty text content
    --   3. element class matches a common error pattern:
    --      "alert-danger", "error", "form-error", "validation-error",
    --      "is-invalid", or similar (locale-agnostic, class-based).
    --   4. <dialog> with text containing locale-agnostic error tokens
    --      ("error", "failed", "invalid", "denied", or their
    --      translations as the implementation sees fit).
    -- The element must be visible (not display: none, not aria-hidden).
    -- Detection runs on DOM mutations, coalesced by
    -- error_coalesce_window so a burst of validation messages
    -- becomes one capture, not many.

@invariant HoverRevealCriteria
    -- A "hover reveal" is captured when:
    --   1. The user's cursor stays over the same element for at least
    --      hover_capture_threshold.
    --   2. During that dwell, a tooltip / popover element became
    --      visible (a new element appeared in the DOM, either from
    --      the title attribute, ARIA describedby, or any descendant
    --      with role = "tooltip" / role = "status").
    --   3. The revealed element has non-empty text content.
    -- Mouse-leave or keyboard activity before the threshold cancels
    -- the capture.

@invariant CaptureGranularity
    -- Exactly one ScoreStep + one TraceSnapshot per accepted firing of
    -- one of the capture rules:
    --   - UserClickCapturesStep
    --   - UserTextInputCapturesStep
    --   - UserSelectionCapturesStep
    --   - UserFileAttachmentCapturesStep
    --   - UserDragDropCapturesStep
    --   - UserMediaPlaybackCapturesStep
    --   - SystemErrorCapturesStep
    -- UserHoverRevealsContent does NOT create a step; it annotates the
    -- last step's note. This is the explicit exception to "one event,
    -- one column".
    --
    -- An "accepted" firing means the Recorder is in state = recording
    -- (paused suspends capture entirely, see PauseSuspendsCapture)
    -- and the kind/trigger combination is permitted by
    -- TriggerMatchesKind.

@invariant TriggerMatchesKind
    -- Each TraceSnapshot has a captured_kind and a captured_trigger.
    -- The combinations the spec permits:
    --   click           with kind in {button, link, generic, drag_source}
    --   text_committed  with kind in {text_input, password_input, text_area}
    --                   or contenteditable=true elements
    --   selection_committed with kind in {dropdown, checkbox, radio}
    --   file_attached   with kind = file_input
    --   drag_drop       with kind = drag_target (the destination)
    --   media_play      with kind = media
    --   system_error    with kind = error_surface
    -- Any other combination is a contract violation, never produced
    -- by the rules in this spec.

@invariant PauseSuspendsCapture
    -- While Recorder.state = paused, NO capture rule fires. Events
    -- that would otherwise trigger a capture are silently dropped.
    -- The recorder is "asleep but not dead": the active_score and
    -- its trace remain intact, and resuming continues to append to
    -- the same trace.

@invariant ScreenshotScope
    -- A captured screenshot is the visible viewport of the active
    -- tab at capture time, encoded as a JPEG data URL. Off-screen
    -- page content is not captured. The focus region marks the
    -- targeted element's bounding box at capture time, normalised
    -- to percentages so the overlay tracks the image as it is
    -- rescaled.

@invariant DialogueValuePrivacy
    -- The dialogue text written into a captured step NEVER contains
    -- the verbatim value typed into a text_input, password_input or
    -- text_area. The verb describes the act ("Escribir en email"),
    -- not the content. For password_input, no aspect of the typed
    -- value (length, characters, shape) is encoded — only the act.
    --
    -- Selection-committed events (dropdown, checkbox, radio) DO
    -- include the chosen option text, because that text is choice
    -- metadata, not free user input.

invariant SingleActiveScore {
    Recorder.state = recording implies exists Recorder.active_score
    Recorder.state = paused    implies exists Recorder.active_score
    Recorder.state = idle      implies Recorder.active_score = null
}

invariant ScoreLibraryCapacity {
    Score.count <= config.score_library_capacity
}

invariant CellLayerCompatibility {
    for s in Scores where layout = pix:
        for m in s.movements:
            for st in m.steps:
                st.environment_cell = empty_cell
                st.supporting_cell = empty_cell
}

invariant StepPositionsAreContiguous {
    for m in Movements:
        for st in m.steps:
            st.position >= 0 and st.position < m.steps.count
}

invariant TraceCardinality {
    -- Score and ScreenshotTrace are 1:1.
    for t in ScreenshotTraces:
        exists t.score
        t.score.trace = t
}

invariant TraceSnapshotMatchesScoreStep {
    for s in TraceSnapshots:
        exists s.step
        s.step.movement.score = s.trace.score
}

@invariant CaptureDerivedFieldsImmutable
    -- Once a TraceSnapshot has been written, no rule modifies any of
    -- its fields. The whole snapshot can be deleted (UserDeletesStep
    -- cascade, UserDeletesTrace, UserDeletesScore) — append-only is
    -- per-field, not per-entity.

@invariant RecordingSurvivesNavigationAndTabs
    -- Top-level navigations in the tab being recorded — including
    -- cross-origin hops, redirects through 3DS flows, and the
    -- eventual return to the original origin — do not change
    -- Recorder.state.
    --
    -- Recording also follows the user across tabs. When a click on
    -- a recorded page opens a new tab (target=_blank, window.open,
    -- middle-click, ctrl-click, "open in new tab" from context
    -- menu), the recorder begins capturing in that new tab against
    -- the same active_score. The first captured snapshot in the new
    -- tab carries boundary = crossing iff the host differs from the
    -- previous snapshot's host (see BoundaryReflectsHostChange) and
    -- captured_tab_id reflects the new tab.
    --
    -- The number of host crossings and tab switches within a single
    -- movement is unbounded.

invariant TabIdentityRecorded {
    -- Every TraceSnapshot records the browser tab where the
    -- capture occurred. The walkthrough viewer can use this to
    -- annotate consecutive snapshots that came from different tabs
    -- (parallel flows in the linear partitura), per
    -- @guarantee TabIdentityVisibleInViewer in walkthrough-viewer.allium.
    for s in TraceSnapshots:
        exists s.captured_tab_id
}

invariant BoundaryReflectsHostChange {
    -- A snapshot's boundary is `crossing` exactly when its
    -- captured_from_url is on a different host than the previous
    -- snapshot's captured_from_url in the same trace.
    for t in ScreenshotTraces:
        for s in t.snapshots:
            let prev = t.snapshots
                .where(p => p.step.position < s.step.position)
                .last
            s.boundary = crossing iff (
                prev != null
                and host_of(prev.captured_from_url) != host_of(s.captured_from_url)
            )
}

invariant SectionStartsOnScreenChange {
    -- A captured ScoreStep has step_title != "" exactly when, vs the
    -- previous captured step in the same movement:
    --   - it is the first step in the movement, OR
    --   - the captured_from_url changed, OR
    --   - the captured_page_title changed, OR
    --   - the captured_tab_id changed (user switched tab and
    --     captured something in the other tab).
    -- Otherwise step_title is empty.
    --
    -- This invariant constrains only the seed value at capture time.
    -- The user can edit step_title freely after capture.
    for m in Movements:
        for st in m.steps where exists snapshot_of(st):
            let snap = snapshot_of(st)
            let prev_step = m.steps.where(p => p.position < st.position).last
            let prev_snap = if prev_step != null: snapshot_of(prev_step) else: null
            let is_section_start =
                prev_step = null
                or prev_snap = null
                or prev_snap.captured_from_url != snap.captured_from_url
                or prev_snap.captured_page_title != snap.captured_page_title
                or prev_snap.captured_tab_id != snap.captured_tab_id
            (st.step_title != "") iff is_section_start
}

invariant ScoreStateTransitionExplicit {
    -- A Score's state changes only via UserMarksScoreAsFinal or
    -- UserReopensScoreAsDraft. No rule mutates state automatically.
}

invariant StableIdsAreUnique {
    for s1, s2 in Scores where s1 != s2:        s1.id != s2.id
    for m1, m2 in Movements where m1 != m2:     m1.id != m2.id
    for st1, st2 in ScoreSteps where st1 != st2: st1.id != st2.id
    for ts1, ts2 in TraceSnapshots where ts1 != ts2: ts1.id != ts2.id
}

-- ============================================================
-- Surfaces
-- ============================================================

surface BrowserHost {
    facing browser: BrowserExtensionRuntime

    exposes:
        UserCreatesScore(layout: ScoreLayout, title: String?)
        UserStartsRecording(score: Score)
        UserPausesRecording
        UserResumesRecording
        UserStopsRecording
        UserStartsNewMovement(score: Score)
        UserAddsBlankStep(movement: Movement)
        UserEditsCell(step: ScoreStep, layer: ScoreLayer, new_value: Cell)
        UserEditsScoreMetadata(score: Score, title: String?, description: String?, layout: ScoreLayout?)
        UserMarksScoreAsFinal(score: Score)
        UserReopensScoreAsDraft(score: Score)
        UserDeletesStep(step: ScoreStep)
        UserDeletesScore(score: Score)
        UserDeletesTrace(score: Score)

        -- Capture event sources (from content scripts):
        UserClicksElement(element: InteractiveElement)
        UserBlursTextInput(element: InteractiveElement, text_changed: Boolean)
        UserChangesSelection(element: InteractiveElement, new_value: String)
        UserAttachesFile(element: InteractiveElement, file_count: Integer, file_names: List<String>)
        UserDragsAndDrops(source: InteractiveElement, target: InteractiveElement)
        MediaElementBeganPlaying(media: MediaElement)
        ErrorBecameVisible(indicator: ErrorIndicator)
        HoverRevealedContent(element: InteractiveElement, revealed_text: String, duration: Duration)

        UserExportsScoreAsPiXJson(score: Score)
        UserExportsScoreAsPdf(score: Score)
        UserImportsPiXScore(document: PiXScoreDocument)

    @guarantee NoNetworkSideEffects
        -- No rule sends data to a remote service. Recordings live
        -- entirely inside browser-local storage.

    @guarantee LocalOnlyPersistence
        -- Scores and screenshot traces persist in browser-local
        -- storage. The canonical home is the editor's IndexedDB.
        -- Scores are not synced across devices and not exposed to
        -- other extensions.

    @guarantee RecordingStateAlwaysVisible
        -- Whenever Recorder.state in {recording, paused}, the user
        -- sees a persistent visual indicator that the recorder is
        -- engaged. Recording and paused are visually distinct (e.g.
        -- pulsing red dot vs steady amber dot). The indicator is
        -- visible on every tab where the recorder might capture.
        -- It disappears only after UserStopsRecording.

    @guarantee CrossSiteCaptureScope
        -- The boundary marker on a TraceSnapshot is metadata only:
        -- it describes that the user crossed hosts since the
        -- previous snapshot. It does not enable broader capture on
        -- the new host. Pages that block content-script injection
        -- (browser-internal pages, certain bank-side iframes) cannot
        -- be captured; recording on them is silent (no step, no
        -- placeholder).

    @guarantee RecordingPersistedOnStop
        -- On UserStopsRecording, the active Score and its
        -- ScreenshotTrace are persisted to the editor's canonical
        -- library. If the editor is unreachable at that moment
        -- (offline, dev server down, prod URL not configured),
        -- the data remains in extension storage as a pending sync
        -- until a successful flush. The recording is never
        -- silently dropped.

    @guarantee PrivacyOfTypedValues
        -- Per @invariant DialogueValuePrivacy: typed text from
        -- text_input, password_input, text_area and contenteditable
        -- never appears in any captured cell. The user can later
        -- enrich the dialogue text in the editor — that's a
        -- post-capture authoring decision, not a capture decision.

    @guarantee ImportRejectionExplained
        -- When UserImportsPiXScore(target, document) is rejected
        -- because target.id != document.score_id, the surface
        -- explains the mismatch and offers a re-export of target
        -- as the recovery path. The extension never silently
        -- creates a new Score from a foreign document.
}

-- ============================================================
-- Open Questions
-- ============================================================

open question "Library overflow at config.score_library_capacity: refuse new scores, evict the oldest, or warn the user?"

open question "Granularity aggregation: should consecutive captures within the same form / component collapse to a single step at capture time (smart-buffering), or always be captured atomically and merged later in the editor (post-capture)? This spec assumes the latter (capture-all-then-merge) — the merge affordance lives in the editor (UserMergesSteps, in score-contract.allium when written)."

open question "Perceptual screen changes that share URL, document.title and tab — e.g. an SPA wizard where a 'cart' has 3 moments rendered in place via JS. SectionStartsOnScreenChange does not detect these. Heuristic options: detect significant DOM mutation, observe history.replaceState, or expose a keyboard shortcut for the user to mark sections while recording. Decision deferred."

open question "user_cell suggestion heuristic: should suggest_user_cell ever return non-empty? This spec returns empty_cell in all cases — the user layer is left blank for the human author to fill in. High-confidence signals (e.g. landing on a confirmation page after a submit -> pix-happy) might be worth seeding. Open."

open question "Re-recording a Score: starting a new recording session against an existing Score (with an existing trace) — replace the previous trace, append-extend it, or forbid? This spec forbids via @invariant TraceCardinality — recording a draft starts fresh. Confirm or relax."

open question "Hover-reveal capture: today HoverRevealCriteria detects tooltips/popovers via DOM mutation during dwell. Some sites render content on hover via CSS-only (no DOM change) — those reveals are invisible to the recorder. Heuristic to detect CSS-only reveals (computed-style change of a specific element) is possible but expensive. Defer."

open question "Media playback scope: today only the first play event per <video>/<audio> element is captured. Should pause / seek / end be captured too? Should re-playing the same element produce a new step? Defer."

open question "Drag-drop screenshot timing: the screenshot is taken at drop. The dragged element is no longer visible in its original position. Should we also capture a snapshot at drag-start (showing the source 'in flight')? That doubles the storage cost per drag-drop. Defer."

open question "Multi-tab parallelism representation: today TraceSnapshot.captured_tab_id annotates each snapshot, and SectionStartsOnScreenChange creates a section divider on tab switch. The partitura is still linear. Should we instead create a separate Movement per tab (parallel branches in the score data model)? Today no — the linear interleaving with tab annotations is the chosen abstraction. Revisit if user testing shows the linear view is confusing."
